==Musical numbers==

;Act I
*1. Opening Chorus and Ballet &ndash; "Lads and lasses round about the hop-pole trip" 
*2. Song with Trio &ndash; "Be wise in time, Oh Phyllis mine" (Dorothy, Lydia, and Phyllis)
*3. Quartet &ndash; "We're sorry to delay you" (Dorothy, Lydia, Wilder, and Sherwood)
*4. Ballad &ndash; "With such a dainty dame none can compare" (Wilder)
*5  Quintet &ndash; "A father's pride and joy they are" (Dorothy, Lydia, Wilder, Sherwood, and Tuppitt)
*6. Song and Trio &ndash; "I am the Sheriff's faithful man" (Lurcher, Wilder, and Sherwood)
*7. Quartet &ndash; "You swear to be good and true" (Dorothy, Lydia, Wilder, and Sherwood)
*8. Chorus with Solo &ndash; "Under the pump" (Lurcher)
*9. Act I Finale &ndash; "Now take your seats at table spread"

;Act II
*10. Act II Introduction and Country Dance 
*11. Song &ndash; "Though born a man of high degree" (Wilder and Chorus)
*12. Music for the Entrance of Dorothy and Lydia 
*13. Graceful Dance 
*14. Song &ndash; "Contentment I give you and all that it brings" (Bantam)
*15. Septet and Chorus &ndash; "Now let's to bed" (Dorothy, Lydia, Wilder, Sherwood, Lurcher, and Bantam)
*16. Recit and Quartett &ndash; "One moment pray" (Dorothy, Lydia, Wilder, and Sherwood)
*16a. Ballad &ndash; "I stand at your threshold sighing" ("Queen of my Heart") (Sherwood)
*17. Trio &ndash; "Are you sure that they are all in bed?" (Wilder, Sherwood, and Bantam)
*18. Chorus with Dorothy, Lydia, Wilder, Sherwood, Bantam, and Lurcher &ndash; "What noise was that" 
*19. Act II Finale &ndash; "Hark forward"

;Act III
*20. Act III &ndash; Ballet 
*21. Chorus &ndash; "Dancing is not what it used to be" 
*22. Ballad &ndash; "The time has come when I must yield" (Phyllis)
*23. Septet and Chorus &ndash; "What joy untold to feel at last" 
*24. Act III Finale &ndash; "You swore to be good and true"

No. 16a became a successful ballad standard, "Queen of My Heart."

